# Keep GitHub's automatic "Source code (zip / tar.gz)" release archives free of
# files that look like something you could import into Collibra.
#
# Those two links are added by GitHub to every release and cannot be removed.
# A technician who downloads one and uploads a workflow.bpmn from it gets a
# workflow that deploys and then fails at its first script task with
# "MissingPropertyException: No such property: <script name>", because the
# .bpmn files in this repository are TEMPLATES: their <script> elements hold
# {{script:...}} placeholders that deploy.py replaces at build time.
#
# export-ignore excludes a path from `git archive`, which is what GitHub uses
# to build those archives (verified against this repository, Sept 2026). The
# release bundles we attach ourselves are unaffected, and so is CI: the release
# workflow checks the repository out with actions/checkout (a git clone), not
# an archive download.
#
# Only the BPMN templates are excluded. The Groovy, forms, docs and tooling stay
# in the archive, so a source snapshot is still a useful source snapshot.
*.bpmn export-ignore
